WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/settings/components/QuietHoursPanel.tsx — the quiet-hours / Do-Not-Disturb GlassPanel that
  CRUDs /notifications/quiet-hours. Each row is a local-time window (HH:MM start + end + IANA timezone), a 7-bit
  weekday mask (Sun=1<<0 … Sat=1<<6), and a bypass-severity allow-list that escapes the gate. Branches:
    1. Loading  — <GlassPanel> header + <Spinner/> "Loading quiet-hours windows…" (placeholder INSIDE the panel
                  chrome so the layout doesn't reflow when data arrives).
    2. Empty    — header + <EmptyState> (Moon glyph + "No quiet-hours windows yet…").
    3. List     — header + <ul> of rows: enabled/disabled Badge + "23:00 → 07:00 (tz)" summary +
                  nextWindowChangeLabel hint + Edit/Delete + all-7 weekday chips (on/off) + bypass Badges.
  The add/edit form (rendered beneath whenever a draft is open) = title (add vs edit) + Enabled Toggle + Start/End
  <input type=time> + timezone <Select> (Intl zones) + weekday toggle buttons + bypass-severity toggle buttons +
  inline validationError + Cancel / Update|Create. validateDraft enforces HH:MM (the `HHMM` regex), start≠end,
  timezone present, weekday mask in (0,127]; the exported pure nextWindowChangeLabel(w, now) emits the next
  state-change label (wrap / non-wrap branches). Hooks: useQuietHours (GET list), useSaveQuietHours (POST/PATCH),
  useDeleteQuietHours (DELETE), useToast (success/error after each mutation), useTranslation. (The optional
  seedDraft/onSeedConsumed AI-advisor prop is a sibling-surface seam, out of scope for this panel.)

